// 2026-08-01 (Phase 3): CLI argv access — RETIRED 2026-09-10 (Family F).
//
// The __argv_* accessors lived in briev_rt.c and had ZERO shipped users;
// their `-> String` frgns were also latently broken (they forwarded raw
// char* — not the [len][bytes] Briev String ABI). Deleted with the C
// runtime (see docs/architecture/briev-native-runtime.md).
//
// CLI argv access returns as an Args# intrinsic over the captured
// argv/environ globals (@__briev_argv / @__briev_environ — both stored by
// the backend-owned _start) when a CLI surface is actually needed. Until
// then, `entry!`/`args!` expansions fail to resolve with a loud
// undefined-symbol error — the honest signal that the surface is retired.
